 "admissions_overview": {
  "summary": "Canada has no national application system: admission is organised by province and decided by each university. In Ontario, the Ontario Universities' Application Centre (OUAC) is a not-for-profit, centralized application service for applicants to Ontario universities, and the universities make the admission decisions. Outside Ontario, you usually apply directly through the university's own online system, for example at Dalhousie or the Université de Montréal, and deadlines vary by program.",
  "official_url": "https://www.ouac.on.ca/",
  "notes": "Application windows, deadlines and program lists change every year and differ by province. Quebec has its own system and French-language programs. Check the university admissions page, and OUAC for Ontario."
 },
